# Corporate events of a fixed list of six listed companies ("issuers"): the days on which each publishes its
# results (earnings releases), holds its annual general meeting (AGM), and the ex-dividend day of its shares.
#
# Translated from holidays-events rules/catalog/issuers.yaml.
#
# How to read a rule: "rule <key> for <event> in <scope> = <dates> with kind = ..., cites ...;" says on which days
# the event <event> happens for the company <scope>. "ANNOUNCED BY <source>" means the company publishes the dates
# itself (in the financial calendar of its investor-relations website); the rule has no dates until it does. With
# "ELSE <dates>" the dates after ELSE are projections used for the years the company has not published yet; the
# published dates always win. "5 MAY > NEXT TUE" is the first Tuesday strictly after 5 May, i.e. the first Tuesday
# on or after 6 May. "@<key>" stands for the dates of another rule, and "> NEXT BD ON exchange:XETR" moves to the
# next business day (strictly after the date) of the Xetra trading calendar. "kind = event" marks a dated event
# that does not change whether the day is a business day. "cites" names the source; "label official" means the
# source is the company itself. The full syntax is in README.md in this directory.
#
# All dates of this file come from the companies themselves. Most rules have no projection at all: without the
# company's announcement there is no date. Two AGMs (Lufthansa and LVMH) follow a pattern regular enough to be
# projected (at least 80 % exact hits on the company's own dates over two years); the ex-dividend day of the three
# German companies with an AGM rule follows from the AGM by German law.
#
# Scopes used in this file (each an issuer, identified by its Legal Entity Identifier, LEI, from GLEIF, the Global
# Legal Entity Identifier Foundation; check digits validated):
#   issuer:7LTWFZYICNSX8D621K86   Deutsche Bank AG, bank, Germany (Europe/Berlin); primary listing Xetra.
#   issuer:529900PH63HYJ86ASW55   Deutsche Lufthansa AG, airline, Germany (Europe/Berlin); primary listing Xetra.
#   issuer:529900K9B0N5BT694847   Allianz SE, insurer, Germany (Europe/Berlin); primary listing Xetra.
#   issuer:851WYGNLUQLFZBSYGB56   Commerzbank AG, bank, Germany (Europe/Berlin); primary listing Xetra.
#   issuer:F3JS33DEI6XQ4ZBPTN86   Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken AB (SEB), bank, Sweden (Europe/Stockholm); primary
#                                 listing Nasdaq Stockholm.
#   issuer:IOG4E947OATN0KJYSD45   LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton SE, luxury goods group, France (Europe/Paris);
#                                 primary listing Euronext Paris.
# Also referred to (declared in de_ez.rules): exchange:XETR, Xetra, the electronic stock trading venue of Deutsche
# Börse in Frankfurt (market identifier code XETR), whose trading days are the business days for the German
# ex-dividend days.
#
# The ex-dividend day under German law: a German stock corporation's dividend falls due at the earliest on the
# third business day after the AGM that resolves it (section 58(4) of the German Stock Corporation Act, AktG); the
# share trades without the dividend ("ex") from the first business day after the AGM. It only happens if the AGM
# resolves a dividend; the rules below cannot know that and give the day every year.


# ===================================================================================================================
# Deutsche Bank AG (issuer:7LTWFZYICNSX8D621K86)
# Who sets the dates: Deutsche Bank, in its investor-relations financial calendar (source ir_deutsche_bank).
# ===================================================================================================================

# Deutsche Bank's results releases (annual and quarterly). Only the dates in its financial calendar count, which is
# usually published about a year ahead; no projection.
rule issuer.deutsche_bank.earnings_release for earnings_release in issuer:7LTWFZYICNSX8D621K86
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_deutsche_bank
  with kind = event
  cites "Deutsche Bank AG investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://investor-relations.db.com/reports-and-events/financial-calendar" label official;

# Deutsche Bank's annual general meeting. Listed in the financial calendar; the formal invitation comes about a
# month ahead. No projection: the date has no regular pattern.
rule issuer.deutsche_bank.agm for agm in issuer:7LTWFZYICNSX8D621K86
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_deutsche_bank
  with kind = event
  cites "Deutsche Bank AG investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://investor-relations.db.com/reports-and-events/financial-calendar" label official;

# Deutsche Bank's ex-dividend day: the first business day after the AGM on the Xetra calendar (German law, see the file
# header; Xetra is where the shares trade in Germany, so its business days decide), only if
# the AGM resolves a dividend. As the AGM has no projected date, this day too exists only once the AGM date is
# announced.
rule issuer.deutsche_bank.ex_dividend for ex_dividend in issuer:7LTWFZYICNSX8D621K86
  = @issuer.deutsche_bank.agm > NEXT BD ON exchange:XETR
  with kind = event, note "only if the AGM resolves a dividend"
  cites "Deutsche Bank AG investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://investor-relations.db.com/reports-and-events/financial-calendar" label official;


# ===================================================================================================================
# Deutsche Lufthansa AG (issuer:529900PH63HYJ86ASW55)
# Who sets the dates: Lufthansa, in its investor-relations financial calendar (source ir_lufthansa).
# ===================================================================================================================

# Lufthansa's results releases (annual and quarterly). Only the dates in its financial calendar count, usually
# published about a year ahead; no projection.
rule issuer.lufthansa.earnings_release for earnings_release in issuer:529900PH63HYJ86ASW55
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_lufthansa
  with kind = event
  cites "Deutsche Lufthansa AG investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://investor-relations.lufthansagroup.com/en/events/financial-calendar.html" label official;

# Lufthansa's annual general meeting. The company announces it in its financial calendar (invitation about a month
# ahead). For the years not announced yet it is projected as the first Tuesday on or after 6 May: an observed
# pattern, not a rule of the company. It held every year since 2022 and in 2019, and missed in 2016, 2017, 2020
# and 2021.
rule issuer.lufthansa.agm for agm in issuer:529900PH63HYJ86ASW55
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_lufthansa ELSE 5 MAY > NEXT TUE
  with kind = event
  cites "Deutsche Lufthansa AG investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://investor-relations.lufthansagroup.com/en/events/financial-calendar.html" label official;

# Lufthansa's ex-dividend day: the first business day after the AGM on the Xetra calendar (German law, see the file
# header; Xetra is where the shares trade in Germany, so its business days decide), only if the
# AGM resolves a dividend. It follows the announced AGM, or the projected
# one (then the Wednesday after it) until the AGM is announced.
rule issuer.lufthansa.ex_dividend for ex_dividend in issuer:529900PH63HYJ86ASW55
  = @issuer.lufthansa.agm > NEXT BD ON exchange:XETR
  with kind = event, note "only if the AGM resolves a dividend"
  cites "Deutsche Lufthansa AG investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://investor-relations.lufthansagroup.com/en/events/financial-calendar.html" label official;


# ===================================================================================================================
# Allianz SE (issuer:529900K9B0N5BT694847)
# Who sets the dates: Allianz, in its investor-relations financial calendar (source ir_allianz).
# ===================================================================================================================

# Allianz's results releases (annual and quarterly). Only the dates in its financial calendar count, usually
# published about a year ahead; no projection.
rule issuer.allianz.earnings_release for earnings_release in issuer:529900K9B0N5BT694847
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_allianz
  with kind = event
  cites "Allianz SE investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://www.allianz.com/en/investor_relations/conferences-presentations/financial-calendar.html"
    label official;

# Allianz's annual general meeting, announced in its financial calendar (invitation about a month ahead). No
# projection.
rule issuer.allianz.agm for agm in issuer:529900K9B0N5BT694847
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_allianz
  with kind = event
  cites "Allianz SE investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://www.allianz.com/en/investor_relations/conferences-presentations/financial-calendar.html"
    label official;

# Allianz's ex-dividend day: the first business day after the AGM on the Xetra calendar (German law, see the file
# header; Xetra is where the shares trade in Germany, so its business days decide), only if the
# AGM resolves a dividend. Exists only once the AGM date is announced.
rule issuer.allianz.ex_dividend for ex_dividend in issuer:529900K9B0N5BT694847
  = @issuer.allianz.agm > NEXT BD ON exchange:XETR
  with kind = event, note "only if the AGM resolves a dividend"
  cites "Allianz SE investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://www.allianz.com/en/investor_relations/conferences-presentations/financial-calendar.html"
    label official;


# ===================================================================================================================
# Commerzbank AG (issuer:851WYGNLUQLFZBSYGB56)
# Who sets the dates: Commerzbank, in its investor-relations financial calendar (source ir_commerzbank). Its server
# omits an intermediate TLS certificate, so automated fetches need that certificate added for the host.
# ===================================================================================================================

# Commerzbank's results releases (annual and quarterly). Only the dates in its financial calendar count, usually
# published about a year ahead; no projection.
rule issuer.commerzbank.earnings_release for earnings_release in issuer:851WYGNLUQLFZBSYGB56
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_commerzbank
  with kind = event
  cites "Commerzbank AG investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://investor-relations.commerzbank.com/financial-calendar" label official;

# Commerzbank's annual general meeting, announced in its financial calendar (invitation about a month ahead). No
# projection.
rule issuer.commerzbank.agm for agm in issuer:851WYGNLUQLFZBSYGB56
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_commerzbank
  with kind = event
  cites "Commerzbank AG investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://investor-relations.commerzbank.com/financial-calendar" label official;

# Commerzbank's ex-dividend day: the first business day after the AGM on the Xetra calendar (German law, see the file
# header; Xetra is where the shares trade in Germany, so its business days decide), only if
# the AGM resolves a dividend. Exists only once the AGM date is announced.
rule issuer.commerzbank.ex_dividend for ex_dividend in issuer:851WYGNLUQLFZBSYGB56
  = @issuer.commerzbank.agm > NEXT BD ON exchange:XETR
  with kind = event, note "only if the AGM resolves a dividend"
  cites "Commerzbank AG investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://investor-relations.commerzbank.com/financial-calendar" label official;


# ===================================================================================================================
# Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken AB, SEB (issuer:F3JS33DEI6XQ4ZBPTN86)
# Who sets the dates: SEB, in its investor-relations financial calendar (source ir_seb).
# ===================================================================================================================

# SEB's results releases (annual and quarterly). Only the dates in its financial calendar count, usually
# published about a year ahead; no projection.
rule issuer.seb.earnings_release for earnings_release in issuer:F3JS33DEI6XQ4ZBPTN86
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_seb
  with kind = event
  cites "Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken AB (SEB) investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://sebgroup.com/investor-relations/reports-and-presentations/financial-calendar" label official;

# SEB's annual general meeting, announced in its financial calendar (invitation about a month ahead). No
# projection.
rule issuer.seb.agm for agm in issuer:F3JS33DEI6XQ4ZBPTN86
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_seb
  with kind = event
  cites "Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken AB (SEB) investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://sebgroup.com/investor-relations/reports-and-presentations/financial-calendar" label official;

# SEB's ex-dividend day. The catalog links it to no other date (the German rule of the file header is German law
# and does not apply to a Swedish company), so only the date SEB publishes (financial calendar or dividend
# announcement) counts; no projection.
rule issuer.seb.ex_dividend for ex_dividend in issuer:F3JS33DEI6XQ4ZBPTN86
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_seb
  with kind = event
  cites "Skandinaviska Enskilda Banken AB (SEB) investor relations financial calendar"
    url "https://sebgroup.com/investor-relations/reports-and-presentations/financial-calendar" label official;


# ===================================================================================================================
# LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton SE (issuer:IOG4E947OATN0KJYSD45)
# Who sets the dates: LVMH, in its financial calendar (source ir_lvmh).
# ===================================================================================================================

# LVMH's results releases (annual and half-year results, quarterly revenue). Only the dates in its financial
# calendar count, usually published about a year ahead; no projection.
rule issuer.lvmh.earnings_release for earnings_release in issuer:IOG4E947OATN0KJYSD45
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_lvmh
  with kind = event
  cites "LVMH investor relations financial calendar" url "https://www.lvmh.com/en/financial-calendar" label official;

# LVMH's annual general meeting. The company announces it in its financial calendar (invitation about a month
# ahead). For the years not announced yet it is projected as the first Thursday on or after 17 April ("16 APR >
# NEXT THU"): an observed pattern, not a rule of the company. It held every year since 2022 and in 2019, and
# missed in 2017, 2018 and 2021.
rule issuer.lvmh.agm for agm in issuer:IOG4E947OATN0KJYSD45
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_lvmh ELSE 16 APR > NEXT THU
  with kind = event
  cites "LVMH investor relations financial calendar" url "https://www.lvmh.com/en/financial-calendar" label official;

# LVMH's ex-dividend day. The catalog links it to no other date (the German rule of the file header is German law
# and does not apply to a French company), so only the date LVMH publishes (financial calendar or dividend
# announcement) counts; no projection.
rule issuer.lvmh.ex_dividend for ex_dividend in issuer:IOG4E947OATN0KJYSD45
  = ANNOUNCED BY ir_lvmh
  with kind = event
  cites "LVMH investor relations financial calendar" url "https://www.lvmh.com/en/financial-calendar" label official;
